Repair self-intersecting STAC item footprints before clipping them in WGS84.

Symptom (Phase 1, --with-s1):
    shapely.errors.GEOSException: TopologyException: side location conflict at
    -118.92514736712955 44.376983527204914. This can occur if the input geometry
    is invalid.
raised from safely_reproject_within_valid_area() via _filter_and_project_items()
-> match_candidate_items_to_window() -> get_items(). Some Sentinel-1 GRD swath
polygons served by Planetary Computer are self-intersecting; GEOS refuses to
intersect them. Sentinel-2 (Element84) footprints are simple boxes, so only the
sentinel1 layer trips this.

Impact without the patch: the exception escapes get_items() for the WHOLE window,
so `rslearn dataset prepare` (which defaults to --ignore-errors) drops the entire
sentinel1 layer from items.json -- all 12 monthly groups, not just the bad scene.
`materialize` then logs "Not materializing layer sentinel1 ... because it is not
prepared" and the tile silently ends up S2-only. Retries do not help: the same
invalid polygon comes back from the STAC API every attempt.

The fix mirrors the fallback shp_intersects() already applies a few lines above in
the same file (geometry.py:42-45) -- it catches shapely.GEOSException there but not
on the .intersection() call that actually throws.

Apply on Bridges-2:
    SITE=/jet/home/kdoerkse/.conda/envs/jpl/lib/python3.11/site-packages
    cp $SITE/rslearn/utils/geometry.py $SITE/rslearn/utils/geometry.py.bak
    patch -p1 -d $SITE < data_processing/rslearn_invalid_geom.patch

Verify:
    python -c "import inspect; from rslearn.utils import geometry; \
        print('make_valid' in inspect.getsource(geometry.safely_reproject_within_valid_area))"

Re-applying after a conda env rebuild is required; `patch` refuses to apply twice.

diff --git a/rslearn/utils/geometry.py b/rslearn/utils/geometry.py
--- a/rslearn/utils/geometry.py
+++ b/rslearn/utils/geometry.py
@@ -/-/ +/-/ @@ def safely_reproject_within_valid_area(
         if not shp_intersects(src_wgs84.shp, valid_wgs84.shp):
             results.append(None)
             continue

         # Clip in WGS84 to the buffered valid area so we only reproject a small piece.
-        clipped_shp = src_wgs84.shp.intersection(get_clip_region())
+        try:
+            clipped_shp = src_wgs84.shp.intersection(get_clip_region())
+        except shapely.GEOSException:
+            # Self-intersecting source footprint (seen on Sentinel-1 GRD swaths):
+            # GEOS raises "side location conflict" rather than returning a result.
+            # Repair the rings and retry, as shp_intersects() does above.
+            repaired = shapely.make_valid(src_wgs84.shp)
+            clipped_shp = repaired.intersection(get_clip_region())
+            # make_valid can emit a GeometryCollection mixing polygons with the
+            # degenerate lines/points it split out. Downstream expects an areal
+            # geometry, so keep only the polygonal parts.
+            if clipped_shp.geom_type == "GeometryCollection":
+                polys = [
+                    g
+                    for g in clipped_shp.geoms
+                    if g.geom_type in ("Polygon", "MultiPolygon")
+                ]
+                clipped_shp = (
+                    shapely.unary_union(polys) if polys else shapely.Polygon()
+                )
+            logger.warning(
+                "repaired invalid source geometry before clipping (was %s)",
+                shapely.is_valid_reason(src_wgs84.shp),
+            )
         if clipped_shp.is_empty:
             results.append(None)
             continue
